# gbg:managed begin v2.0.0-rc.10 — rewritten by `gbg sync`; do not edit
.gbg/scratch/
docs/build/
docs/Manifest.toml
test/Manifest.toml
benchmark/Manifest.toml
.claude/settings.local.json
*.cov
# gbg:managed end

.ipynb_checkpoints/
Manifest.toml
benchmark/results/
examples/output/
examples/gpu/rocm/output/
docs/build/
docs/site/
docs/src/architecture.md
docs/src/decisions.md
docs/src/formalization.md
docs/src/testing.md
docs/src/performance.md
docs/src/gbg-rules.md
docs/src/gbg-readers.md
docs/src/gbg-instruments.md
docs/src/examples/

# Local-only reference material (theses, papers, notes) — never committed
inspiration/

# /check-consistency findings piles — ephemeral working notes, regenerated each run.
# The instrument itself IS tracked: .claude/commands/check-consistency/ and the
# do-not-re-flag list .claude/doc-review-adjudicated.md, which panel.js reads.
.claude/doc-review/
.claude/doc-review-prev/

# Julia coverage output (`--code-coverage` writes <file>.jl.<pid>.cov beside the source).
# The per-method ledger in test/exhaustive/ runs the value lane under coverage twice, so a run
# leaves hundreds of these. They are stale the moment anything is renamed and nothing reads
# them back. This rule predates the untracking below: it was added while 508 of them were
# already tracked, and .gitignore does not untrack what git already knows about.
*.cov
